.TH OCR\-TELA 1 "2026-08-27" "ocr-tela 1.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ocr\-tela \- copy text from a region of the screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ocr\-tela
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ocr\-tela
freezes the screen, dims it and lets you drag a rectangle over the text you
want. On release the selected region is recognized locally by
.BR tesseract (1)
and the resulting text is placed on the clipboard.
.PP
Nothing is displayed after the selection and no image is kept on disk. Press
.B Esc
to cancel; a click without dragging is treated as a cancellation too.
.PP
The screen capture goes through the
.I org.freedesktop.portal.Screenshot
desktop portal, which is the only way to read the screen under Wayland.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OCR_LANG
Tesseract languages, defaults to
.BR por .
Use for example
.B por+eng
for mixed text, at roughly 40% more time.
.TP
.B OCR_NOTIFY
Set to
.B 0
to suppress the confirmation notification.
.TP
.B OCR_DIM
Dimming applied outside the selection, from 0 to 1. Defaults to 0.45.
.TP
.B OCR_MAX_SIDE
Crops longer than this many pixels are scaled down before recognition.
Defaults to 1400.
.TP
.B OCR_TESSDATA
Alternative directory of tesseract models. Empty, the default, uses the
models installed on the system.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success and when the selection is cancelled, 1 when the screen
could not be captured.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ocr\-tela\-atalho (1),
.BR ocr\-warmup (1),
.BR tesseract (1),
.BR wl\-copy (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Augusto Mateus
